# Stream Input with Node.js readline

For interactive command-line applications or streaming very large datasets that cannot fit entirely in memory, Node.js provides the `readline` module:

```javascript
const readline = require('readline');

const rl = readline.createInterface({
  input: process.stdin,
  output: process.stdout
});

rl.on('line', (line) => {
  console.log(`Received: ${line}`);
});

rl.on('close', () => {
  console.log('Finished processing input.');
});
```

### Key Events
- **`line`**: Emitted whenever the input stream receives an end-of-line character (`\n` or `\r\n`).
- **`close`**: Emitted when `process.stdin` receives EOF.

