# Parsing Numbers and Multi-Line Arrays

Online judges typically format inputs as space-separated tokens or multiple lines:

### Common Patterns

1. **Two Integers on One Line**: `"15 25"`
```javascript
const [a, b] = line.trim().split(/\s+/).map(Number);
```

2. **Array of Numbers Following Size N**:
```javascript
const lines = input.trim().split('\n');
const n = parseInt(lines[0], 10);
const arr = lines[1].trim().split(/\s+/).map(Number);
```

3. **Fast Tokenizer for Mixed Tokens**:
```javascript
const tokens = input.trim().split(/\s+/);
let ptr = 0;
const nextToken = () => tokens[ptr++];
const nextInt = () => parseInt(tokens[ptr++], 10);
```

